# See tests/check.rs `c7_parseback_gate_polarity`.
#
# C7 is a pipeline-integrity gate: no valid-source input can produce TriG
# that fails to re-parse to the same dataset, so its failing polarity is
# exercised at unit level against tampered emitted bytes (this file is the
# tampered-payload artifact the test's corrupted-slice pivot stands in for).
# Replacing the compiled graph.trig with this would instead trip C6 (byte
# drift), not C7 — drift is the CI gate; C7 protects the emitter itself.
tampered payload
